CORE
main.c
--allow-pointer-unsoundness --32 --no-assertions --datarace --unwind 2 --rounds 2 --no-por
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[.*\] datarace: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
precondition_instance.*FAILURE
--
The only read of g is inside a check, and a thread writes g. Under --datarace
--no-assertions the check is made true, but its condition is still evaluated
(into the dummy variable), so the read keeps its event and the race is found.
Making the check true without keeping its condition lost the race.
